20397], "Is it important to drink water? Why?": [1424640, 19053], "It is a sunny day today, but tomorrow it will rain.": [1443693, 28461], "It is half past two": [1472154, 14061], "It is ten past three.": [1486215, 15213], "Mama is cooking rice with chicken. Dinner will be ready at eight.": [1501428, 29613], "My mother is a teacher.": [1531041, 13101], "My phone is new. I bought it last week.": [1544142, 23469], "Nice names! Do you live with all of them?": [1567611, 19437], "Nice names! Do you live with your family?": [1587048, 19437], "Nice to meet you, Aida! How old are you?": [1606485, 19053], "Nice to meet you, Babacar! Where are you from?": [1625538, 22125], "Nice! Senegal is a beautiful country. How old are you?": [1647663, 27693], "Nice! What do you like to do for fun?": [1675356, 17517], "Please give me a stamped receipt as proof.": [1692873, 21549], "Please speak slowly": [1714422, 12909], "Please turn off your phone. The film is starting.": [1727331, 22701], "Road": [1750032, 5421], "Sun cream": [1755453, 8877], "Thank you very much": [1764330, 11565], "That is great! Where do you live?": [1775895, 15405], "That is so lovely! Who is your favorite person in your family?": [1791300, 27885], "That is wonderful! Are you married?": [1819185, 16365], "That is wonderful! Do you play every day?": [1835550, 20013], "That's great! Where do you live, Aida?": [1855563, 17325], "That's nice! How many brothers and sisters do you have?": [1872888, 24813], "That's nice! What are their names?": [1897701, 15981], "The doctor told me to rest and drink water.": [1913682, 23853], "The library is open.": [1937535, 14445], "The market closes at six o'clock today because of the holiday.": [1951980, 33645], "The water is cold, but the soup is hot. Be careful.": [1985625, 28461], "This phone has a twelve-month warranty.": [2014086, 19629], "To buy": [2033715, 8301], "To sell": [2042016, 8109], "To travel": [2050125, 9453], "Today is Monday. The shop opens at eight and closes at five.": [2059578, 35949], "We eat together on Sunday": [2095527, 15981], "We live in a small house in Thiès.": [2111508, 17517], "We live together": [2129025, 11373], "Welcome": [2140398, 8301], "What can you buy at a market?": [2148699, 13485], "What do you buy at the shop?": [2162184, 11949], "What do you do when you are ill?": [2174133, 13485], "What do you like to eat in the morning?": [2187618, 14253], "What time do you get up?": [2201871, 11373], "What time does the class start?": [2213244, 14061], "Where can I rent chairs and tents?": [2227305, 18285], "Where do you buy medicine in your town?": [2245590, 15981], "Where is the pharmacy?": [2261571, 14061], "Where is the town hall?": [2275632, 14253], "Who cleans your home?": [2289885, 10221], "Why is that important to you?": [2300106, 14253], "Wife": [2314359, 5997], "Wonderful! Are you the oldest in your family?": [2320356, 20397], "Wonderful! Is your family big?": [2340753, 16365], "Worker": [2357118, 8301], "You should go to the pharmacy if the pain continues.": [2365419, 24045], "NOTICE TO PASSENGERS. From Monday 4 March, the 08:10 train to Central Station will leave from Platform 3 instead of Platform 1. Tickets bought online can be shown on your phone. Bicycles are not allowed before 09:30. The ticket office is closed on Sundays, but machines are available all day.": [2389464, 183597], "Many cities are building more cycle lanes to reduce traffic. In one city, the number of people cycling to work doubled in five years, and local shops reported that cyclists visit more often than drivers. However, some residents complain that the new lanes reduce parking space. The council says it will review the plan next year.": [2573061, 183405], "Good morning, Palm Hotel. How can I help you? Hello, I would like to book a room for two nights, from Friday the twelfth. A double room costs sixty euros a night, and breakfast is included. Is there parking? Yes, parking is free for guests. Great, my name is Sara Diallo. I will pay by card.": [2756466, 162669], "Attention all students. The library will open one hour earlier during exam week, at seven in the morning, and it will stay open until midnight. Group study rooms must be booked online, at least a day in advance. Please remember that food is not allowed in the reading area, but you can use the cafeteria on the ground floor.": [2919135, 181485], "Hello, my name is Amina. I am twenty-eight years old. I live in London with my husband and my son. My son is four. I work in a shop on Saturdays.": [3100620, 86829], "Hello, I have an appointment with Doctor Brown at half past ten. My name is Omar Sy. I have a bad cough and a headache since Monday. Please sit down, the doctor is a little late. He will see you in about fifteen minutes.": [3187449, 123885], "I am calling about the flat you advertised. Is it still available? Yes, it is. It has two bedrooms and costs nine hundred pounds a month, including water. I would like to visit it on Thursday after work, around six. That is fine, but please bring a document with your address, and we also ask for one month of deposit.": [3311334, 178413], "CAFE LUNA. Soup of the day: 3 euros. Chicken sandwich: 6 euros. Vegetable pasta: 7 euros. Orange juice or tea: 2 euros. All sandwiches come with a free drink before 2 pm. The kitchen closes at 9 pm. We do not take cards for bills under 5 euros.": [3489747, 173421], "Hi team, the Monday meeting is moved to Tuesday at 10:30 because the manager is travelling. Please bring your sales reports. We will meet in Room 4, not in the main office. Lunch will be provided. If you cannot come, tell Anna before Monday evening. Thanks, Paul.": [3663168, 156333], "A study of 600 students found that those who slept eight hours or more scored higher in maths tests than those who slept six hours. Researchers also noticed that students who used phones in bed took longer to fall asleep. Some schools are now starting lessons later in the morning. Teachers say it is too early to know if this improves results.": [3819501, 194157], "VOLUNTEERS NEEDED. The town library is looking for ten volunteers to help with a reading club for children aged six to nine. The club meets every Wednesday from 4 pm to 5 pm. No experience is necessary, but volunteers must be over eighteen and attend a short training session on Saturday 9 June. In return, volunteers receive a free library card and a certificate.": [4013658, 216237], "Remote work has grown quickly in the past decade. A survey of 1,000 employees found that two thirds felt more productive at home, although many missed informal contact with colleagues. Managers were less positive: nearly half said it was harder to train new staff remotely. Some companies have introduced hybrid models, requiring employees in the office for two days a week.": [4229895, 210477], "Many coastal cities face a growing water shortage. Rainfall has become less predictable, and rising demand from industry puts further pressure on supply. Engineers argue that fixing leaking pipes could save up to a third of the water currently lost. However, repairs are expensive, and officials often prefer to build new reservoirs, which attract more public attention. Experts recommend combining both approaches.": [4440372, 232557], "Good morning, Dr Evans' office. Hello, I would like to make an appointment for my son. What is the problem? He has a sore throat and a high temperature since yesterday. I can offer you Thursday at 4:15. Is there anything earlier? Yes, tomorrow at 9:30. That is perfect. Please bring his health card. Thank you very much.": [4672929, 184557], "Excuse me, how do I get to the post office? Go straight on for two hundred metres, then turn left at the bank. The post office is next to the pharmacy, opposite the park. Is it far? No, it takes about five minutes on foot. Does it open on Saturdays? Yes, but only until noon. Thank you. You are welcome.": [4857486, 169581], "Welcome to FitZone. We have two memberships. The basic one costs twenty-five euros a month and includes the gym and the swimming pool. The premium one costs forty euros and also includes classes such as yoga and dance. Students get a ten percent discount if they show a card. There is no contract, so you can stop at any time with one month's notice. The first visit is free.": [5027067, 202221], "Here is the weather for the weekend. Saturday will begin with heavy rain in the north, but the sky will clear by the afternoon and temperatures will reach twenty-two degrees. On Sunday, expect strong winds along the coast, so ferry services may be cancelled. Inland, it will stay dry and sunny. Drivers are advised to take care on mountain roads early on Monday, where frost is possible.": [5229288, 211629], "Welcome to the course on urban planning. Today we will look at three issues: housing, transport and green space. First, I want to stress that these are connected: a city that builds housing far from jobs creates traffic. Over the next six weeks, you will write one short report and give one group presentation. The report counts for sixty percent of your mark. Attendance is not marked, but the presentations cannot be repeated.": [5440917, 223725], "In this week's episode we ask whether artificial intelligence will replace teachers. Our guest, a researcher, argues that technology can handle routine tasks such as marking quizzes, but not the human side of teaching: motivation, trust and encouragement. She adds that schools in rural areas could benefit most, since a tool can offer extra practice where qualified teachers are scarce. However, she warns that tools should be tested carefully before they are widely adopted.": [5664642, 280749]}